WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:07.320
So a lot of people write in and ask the difference
between the question "why" and the WHY,

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.480
as we talk about it, like start with WHY.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:16.200
The WHY is a purpose, cause, or belief,
the underlying reason why we are motivated

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.470
to do something.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.550
The reason a company exists, the reason why
we're passionate for something.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.100
The question "why" aims to get at and assert
the same thing in a generic sense,

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:28.859
like why do you do something, what's the underlying
reason for that?

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:31.689
That's why I called the WHY, "the WHY."

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:37.100
Another reason why I called the WHY "the WHY"
is because when I would ask people,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.110
"What comes first: vision or mission?"

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.110
People would debate it.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.320
There's no standardized definition of vision
or mission.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.780
So people who believe mission came first,
I asked them, "So what's the definition of mission?"

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.120
They said, "It's why we get out
of bed in the morning."

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.350
People who believed vision comes first would
say," Well, it's why our company exists."

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.820
And whether it's brand or purpose, all these
things, everybody gave me the same definition:

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.820
why.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.600
So that's why I called it the WHY.

